    "text": "By Staff Report From Georgia CEO ,\n1 days ago The Institute for Health Logistics & Analytics (IHLA) at Georgia Southern University has opened a new Care Station in the lobby of the Dr. Mark and Tonya Spivey Public Library in Vidalia, Georgia. The Care Station is a health vending machine that aims to improve community health by increasing access to over-the-counter health products and at-home diagnostic tests. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
